#
# Copy this file to docker/.env and fill it in:
#
#     cp docker/.env.example docker/.env
#     chmod 600 docker/.env
#
# docker/start.sh reads docker/.env only when it is mode 0600, since it holds
# keys, and docker compose reads it for the values below. It is never
# committed (docker/.gitignore), and it is left out of every image build
# (docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore). Each value reaches only the containers
# docker/compose.yaml hands it to.

# --- the model provider: required -----------------------------------------------
# The key docker/robinauts.toml reads, by the name its [model_providers] table
# gives. Anthropic is the default there; the file says how to use OpenRouter or
# OpenAI instead, with the key below that goes with each.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- GitHub: for the sandboxed agents ---------------------------------------------
# The token the coder agent reaches GitHub's MCP server with. Only the sandbox
# container gets it: the control plane never does. A fine-grained token,
# limited to the repositories the agent may work on, is the one to give it.
ROBINAUTS_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# --- made by docker/start.sh when they are empty ----------------------------------
# The token the sandbox workers present to the worker API, which the control
# plane checks on every call. docker/start.sh writes a random one here on its
# first run; set your own, of 32 characters or more, if you like.
ROBINAUTS_SANDBOX_TOKEN=
# The password of the database, which only the control plane can reach. It
# goes into a URL, so one of your own is letters and digits alone.
ROBINAUTS_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# --- optional ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the interface is, on this machine's loopback interface alone.
# ROBINAUTS_PORT=8000
